[Music]  hey everyone its Johanna here one of the  best ways to stay on track with a  fitness goal is to male prep whether  your goal is to loose weight put on  weight perhaps you are preparing for a  competition or you just want to stay fit  your daily males contribute 80% to your  success so what you eat matters what  exactly is meal prepping it is basically  preparing and planning your meals in  advance for the entire week so basically  making your own healthy and delicious  pre-packed meals instead of buying them  or eating out some of the benefits  include keeping you on track with your  fitness goal so you have no excuses not  to eat healthy secondly it eliminates  the stress of having to cook for every  single meal especially if you are a busy  mom work in person or busy student but  you get to save money and time not only  will you be saving money by not eating  out  you will also be saving on your gas and  electricity bills  by cooking in box and finally you get to  eat your own healthy and delicious meals  throughout the week so let's go through  the five easy steps to meal prep first  check your schedule and decide how many  days and how many meals do you want to  prep in advance for me I will go with  500 days and I will prep all my meals in  advance perhaps you might only want to  prep your lunch and snacks in advance  and have freshly cooked dinners well it  is entirely up to you and your schedule  the second step decide what you want to  eat be specific and write your meal plan  are you having three larger meals or are  you having five to six smaller meals for  this I will be using my eight-week  bikini body challenge meal plan which is  also available on my website so once you  know exactly what you will be having for  the entire week  go out there and get all the ingredients  you need and also get enough food  containers to store your meals try to  get them in similar shape and sizes so  that it will be easier for you to stack  them up in the fridge or freezer and  make sure that they are freezer and  microwave friendly once you have all  your ingredients ready the next  important step is to weigh and measure  your food this is especially important  if you are new to eating clean and you  are unsure about portion sizes where  your food will allow you to visually see  how large a portion should be and you  will know how many calories is in your  meal so what you need is a food scale  and also measuring cups and spoons I  prefer to weigh my ingredients prior to  cooking because depending on how I cook  how much water I use it may be different  from your meal after cooking and the  final step is to cook and have fun keep  it simple  remember that meal prepping should be  time efficient stress-free fun and easy  so pick easy and delicious recipes to  prep let's cook so here's my meal plan  breakfast  dreamy oatmeal snack peanut butter  energy bar lunch tomorrow rice and beans  snack banana muffins dinner baked salmon  with sweet potato and carrots and also a  side of creamy green soup and I'll be  prepping all this in 2 hours and 30  minutes let's start by making meals that  takes of the longest to cook  I'll start by cooking my rice an easy  tip to cook brown rice is to soak them  at least 4 hours or overnight so that  they will be soft and cook quicker next  peel and chop all the vegetables where  them if you need to this is the most  time-consuming process for me as I'm  rather slow at chopping it'll take me at  least 30 minutes to get this done place  all the vegetables in separate bowls for  easy cooking we want to be doing at  least two things together to save time  so start by preheating the oven first on  the list is to prep my dinner baked  salmon with sweet potatoes and carrots  as they will take 45 minutes to cook in  the oven  salmon is my protein and healthy fat  carrots my vegetable and sweet potato my  complex carbs once it's ready cook this  in the oven for 45 minutes when that's  cooking next is to make the banana  muffins as they will need to cook in the  oven as well combine all the mixtures  together separate them into chopped  muffin cups and once they're ready there  should be about 50 minutes cooking time  left on the oven place this on the top  part of the oven so right now I'm having  two Mills cooking at the same time in  the oven next on the list to cook the  creamy green soup and also tomato rice  with beans cut two parts with olive oil  one to make the creamy green soup and  another for the tomato rice and beans  while those ingredients are cooking in  the pots by now my salmon and banana  muffins will be done take them out of  the oven and allow them to cool down  okay  back onto the stove the beans and  vegetables should be done by now because  my pot is tiny I will transfer the beans  and vegetables into my rice pot and  combine all the ingredients together  lunch is now ready and set it aside to  cool down by now my soup will be ready  for blending removed from heat and plan  all the ingredients until smooth and  creamy done again set it aside to cool  down so now that all the time consuming  meals are ready I'll move on to the  easier meals peanut butter snack bar and  dreamy oatmeal both requires less than  ten minutes to prep combined peanut  butter honey oats and seeds  once that's done press it down firmly  into a square container and place it in  the fridge to cool down and harden  before slicing finally let's make  breakfast  I only prep my breakfast two days in  advance as I do not like my oats to be  too soggy so two layers of oats with two  layers of fruits my dreamy oats are now  ready to go into the fridge overnight  time to pack my meals up for five days  this is the most satisfying part of the  process  so here are my healthy prepared meals  for five days this is an example of my  meals in a day aim to have a balance of  carbs protein vegetables fruits and  healthy fat in your meals as a general  guideline you can't keep your meals in  the fridge for up to two days and you  can freeze them up for up to one week to  warm your food up the easiest way is to  warm it up in a microwave if you do not  want to use a microwave then transfer it  into a bowl and steam it up so pick one  day in a week where you will have the  time to run your meal plan go out and do  your grocery shopping come back and cook  your meals it only took me two and a  half hours to prep my meals for the  entire week so try meal prepping out to  stay on track with a fitness goal don't  forget to snap a picture and share with  me on Instagram or Facebook for new  Fitness food and motivational videos  please like share and subscribe to my  You Tube channel and website do you  follow me on Facebook Instagram and  Twitter to stay connected with me thanks  guys  [Music]

